                      (    forth6809.asm):04473                                   ; UNLOOP discarding 6 of the 8 bytes itself,
                      (    forth6809.asm):04474                                   ; then EXITUNLOOP unconditionally discarding
                      (    forth6809.asm):04475                                   ; a full 8 more, overshooting into whatever
                      (    forth6809.asm):04476                                   ; sat below (typically the caller's own
                      (    forth6809.asm):04477                                   ; return address) and branching into random
                      (    forth6809.asm):04478                                   ; memory on return. Since UNLOOP has no
                      (    forth6809.asm):04479                                   ; other legitimate use than immediately
                      (    forth6809.asm):04480                                   ; preceding an exit from the definition, and
                      (    forth6809.asm):04481                                   ; EXIT already handles that correctly on its
                      (    forth6809.asm):04482                                   ; own, UNLOOP is now a true no-op rather than
